# Defining `to(String)` for one type must not take the conversion away from
# every other type. `42.to(String)` is the universal value conversion the
# prelude owns; the local implementation below only covers Ticket.
#
# KNOWN BEAM DIVERGENCE: the walker answers "42" here, but BEAM raises
# `function_clause` — the local `to/2` shadows the prelude's without falling
# through to it. `make spec-beam` lists this file for that reason; it is a
# real bug in the argument-overloaded dispatch path, not a spec that needs
# relaxing. The same root cause is why a second `to(String)` in the PRELUDE
# silently rerouted every prelude type's conversion — see
# spec/prelude_to_string_dispatch.kex, which guards that half.
record Ticket do
  id : Integer
end

make Ticket do
  let to(String) -> String = "ticket #${this.id}"
end

main do
  IO.printLine(Ticket { id: 7 }.to(String))
  IO.printLine("${42.to(String).or("?")}")
  IO.printLine("${3.5.to(String).or("?")}")
end
